: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. A,C,B are collinear [01] & F,D,E are collinear [04] & AB ∥ DE [02] ⇒  ∠ACE = ∠FEC [10]
002. CA = CB [00] & FE = FD [05] ⇒  CA:CB = FE:FD [11]
003. AE ∥ BD [03] & A,C,B are collinear [01] & F,D,E are collinear [04] & CA:CB = FE:FD [11] ⇒  CF ∥ AE [12]
004. AE ∥ CF [12] ⇒  ∠AEC = ∠FCE [13]
005. ∠ACE = ∠FEC [10] & ∠AEC = ∠FCE [13] (Similar Triangles)⇒  EA = CF [14]
006. A,C,B are collinear [01] & AE ∥ CF [12] ⇒  ∠CAE = ∠BCF [15]
007. CA = CB [00] & EA = CF [14] & ∠CAE = ∠BCF [15] (SAS)⇒  ∠ACE = ∠CBF [16]
008. G,C,E are collinear [06] & H,B,F are collinear [08] & ∠ACE = ∠CBF [16] & A,C,B are collinear [01] ⇒  GE ∥ HF [17]
009. A,D,G are collinear [07] & A,H,D are collinear [09] ⇒  D,G,H are collinear [18]
010. GE ∥ HF [17] & D,G,H are collinear [18] & F,D,E are collinear [04] ⇒  FD:FE = HD:HG [19]
011. FD:FE = HD:HG [19] & FD = FE [05] ⇒  HD = HG
